Emmett, you asked for an honest answer and here it is. VAA concurs with del=
eting Section 09 05 61 from the lobby interiors package.<br />
<br />
Nine in-situ probes read 79 to 83 percent RH against our specified threshol=
d of 85 percent, and Dean Farago's independent probes confirmed the range. =
The section was written into the package as a precaution before anyone had =
tested this slab. The testing says the precaution is unnecessary, so it com=
es out. We are not asking the trust to buy protection against a condition t=
hat does not exist here.<br />
<br />
To be explicit about the record, because these things get read years later.=
 This is not an owner directed deletion over the architect's objection. It =
is a deletion the architect recommends on the basis of the test data, and t=
here is nothing for the trust to acknowledge or accept, because nothing is =
being waived. Take the $126,400 credit and the two weeks with a clear consc=
ience. I will issue the ASI once Marchmont confirms the credit.